00:57:16,363 --> 00:57:22,363
Brothers is a 2009 American psychological thriller film directed
by Jim Sheridan and written by David Benioff.

13
01:02:02,727 --> 01:02:08,727
The film is a remake of the 2004 Danish film by Susanne Bier, and both
films take inspiration from the epic poem Odyssey by Homer.

14
01:06:49,090 --> 01:06:55,090
The film stars Tobey Maguire, Jake Gyllenhaal, Natalie Portman, Sam
Shepard, Clifton Collins Jr., and Mare Winningham.

15
01:11:35,454 --> 01:11:41,454
The film follows Captain Sam Cahill, a USMC officer who is captured by the
Taliban after he is presumably killed in the war in Afghanistan.

16
01:16:21,818 --> 01:16:27,818
Upon being rescued and reunited with his brother Tommy and wife Grace, he
suffers from severe PTSD as he struggles to reintegrate into society.

17
01:21:08,181 --> 01:21:14,181
Brothers was theatrically released in the United States on December 4, 2009, by Lionsgate, and
received mixed reviews from critics, although Maguire's acting was praised.

18
01:25:54,545 --> 01:26:00,545
The film grossed $45 million against a $26 million budget.

19
01:30:40,909 --> 01:30:46,909
The film was nominated for Best Actor for Maguire and Best Original Song for
"Winter", performed by U2, at the 67th Golden Globe Awards.

20
01:35:27,272 --> 01:35:33,272
The film explores themes of sibling relationship, loss of loved one,
brother-in-law, afghanistan war (2001-2021), remake.

21
01:40:13,636 --> 01:40:19,636
The tone is emotional and intense.
